  {
   "id": "L0.1",
   "unit": 0,
   "title": "Shva: silent or vocal",
   "unlocks": [],
   "body": "The shva (two dots stacked under a letter) is either silent or a very short e. The\ntransliteration writes a vocal shva as e and leaves a silent one out.\n\nVocal at the start of a word: {0}, {1}.\n\nSilent when it closes a syllable after a short vowel: {2} has both, a vocal\none under the first letter and a silent one under the bet.\n\nAfter the \"and\" of a story verb the shva is always vocal: {3}.\n\nRule of thumb: start of word, or after a long vowel, sound it; after a short vowel, stay silent.\nTap any word to check yourself.",
   "refs": [
    {
     "ids": [
      "01EVS"
     ],
     "hl": null
    },
