  {
   "id": "L0.2",
   "unit": 0,
   "title": "Dagesh: hard letter or doubled letter",
   "unlocks": [],
   "body": "A dot inside a letter has two jobs.\n\nBet, kaf and pe are hard with the dot (b, k, p) and soft without it (v, kh, f):\n{0} has a hard b and a soft kh; {1} starts with a soft v.\n\nAfter a vowel, the dot doubles the letter. Doubled letters are written twice:\n{2}, {3}.\n\nBoth in one word: {4}, a doubled k and then a soft kh.",
   "refs": [
    {
     "ids": [
