  {
   "id": "L0.3",
   "unit": 0,
   "title": "Qamats: a or o",
   "unlocks": [],
   "body": "The qamats (a small T under the letter) is usually a: {0}, {1}.\n\nIn a closed syllable without stress it is a short o (qamats qatan): {2},\n{3}. A few words are o by tradition: {4}.\n\nThe printed text uses one sign for both. The app decides from syllables and stress, and the\ntransliteration always shows which reading it chose.",
